  "english": "...is risen. And see the rest according to the order in the First Volume until the end, keeping the order of this place.\n\nDecember\n1. Monday. Tone 6 [GK]. Bishop Gennadius and the warrior Mercurius, and James and Iravaphar.\n2. Tuesday. Tone 7 [DK]. Cornelius the Centurion, and Simeon the kinsman of Christ, Polycarp the Patriarch, and the Eastern Martyrs.\n3. Wednesday. Tone 8 [DK]. Fast. Lenten Fathers Tone 8 [DK]: \"Blessed art thou, Lord God of our fathers.\"\n7. Sunday. Tone 4 [BK]. Third [Sunday]. Barekendan of the Fast of Saint James. Fathers Tone 3 [BZ]: \"Who art King.\" Resurrection Hour Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [BK]: \"They anticipated.\"\n9. Tuesday. Tone 6 [GK]. Fast. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin by Anna.\n14. Sunday. Tone 3 [BDZ]. Fourth [Sunday]. Fathers Tone 4 [BK]: \"Who [sent] the servant.\" Resurrection Hour Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 3 [BZ]: \"Today the [multitudes of angels] rejoiced.\"\n...\n21. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADZ]. Fifth [Sunday]. Fathers Tone 5 [GDZ]: \"Who from eternity.\" Resurrection Hour Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [AK]: \"The Risen,\" and \"Wonderful,\" and \"Marvelous.\"\n22. Monday. Tone 3 [BDZ]. Abraham and Khoren, and Cosmas and Damian, and the martyr Adeodatus [Astuadzatur]. Fathers Tone 2 [AK]: \"Holy God, Creator of eternity.\"\n23. Tuesday. Tone 4 [BK]. David the Prophet, and James the Apostle.\n28. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADZ]. Sixth [Sunday]. Fathers Tone 6 [GK]: \"Before eternity.\" Resurrection Hour Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 1 [ADZ]: \"Awesome vision,\" to the end.\n29. Monday. Tone 2 [AK]. James and John. Barekendan of the Nativity.\n30. Tuesday. Tone 3 [BDZ]. Fast of the Nativity of Christ. Lenten Fathers Tone 6 [GK]: \"God of our fathers, praised art thou.\"\n\nJanuary\n4. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Seventh [Sunday], in the midst of the Fast. Resurrection Hour Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [GK]: \"Glory to the resurrection,\" to the end.\n5. Monday. Tone 1 [ADZ]. Eve of the Nativity of Christ. End of the year.\n\nJune\n29. Sunday. Tone 3 [BDZ]. Vardavar [Transfiguration]. The eating period [between fasts] is six weeks. See everything of this interval up to the Holy Cross in the First Year-book, only keeping the calendar date one number higher.\n\nAugust\n17. Sunday. Tone 4 [BK]. Assumption of the Holy Mother of God. The eating period [between fasts] is three weeks. See the feasts of this interval in the First Volume.\n\nSeptember\n7. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADZ]. Fourth [Sunday]. Barekendan of the Holy Cross. Fathers Tone 6 [GK]: \"Ineffable.\" Resurrection Hour Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 1 [ADZ]: \"With the women.\"\n8. Monday. Tone 2 [AK]. Fast of the Holy Cross. Feast of the Birth of the Holy Virgin from Anna.\n9. Tuesday. Tone 3 [BDZ]. Fast. Fathers Tone 5 [GDZ]: \"Glorified name.\"\n14. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Exaltation of the Holy Cross. See from the tenth Sunday in the First Volume; but look up the Fathers of the martyrs and fasts, the Resurrection Hour Hymns [Hambartsi], and those of the days in the First Year-book, only keeping the calendar dates.\n\nNovember\n16. Sunday. Tone 7 [DDZ]. Tenth [Sunday]. Barekendan of the Advent [Yisnak]. Resurrection Hour Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [GDZ]: \"Who art above,\" to the end.\n17. Monday. Tone 8 [DK]. Fast of Advent [Yisnak]. Fathers Tone 7 [DDZ]: \"Who didst show in all.\"\n21. Friday. Tone 4 [BK]. Fast. Feast of the Presentation of the three-year-old Holy Mother of God.\n23. Sunday. Tone 6 [GK]. First [Sunday of Advent]. Fathers Tone 1 [ADZ]: \"Blessed art thou, Lord God.\" Resurrection Hour Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [GK]: \"Thy resurrection,\" and \"Taking.\"\n24. Monday. Tone 7 [DDZ]. The Virgins Juliana and Vasilouhi. Fathers Tone 8 [DK]: \"Those who hope.\"\n30. Sunday. Tone 5 [GDZ]. Second [Sunday of Advent]. Fathers Tone 2 [AK]: \"Unoriginate Word.\" Resurrection Hour Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [GDZ]: \"Glorified.\"",
